WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.610
It was completely
unexpected and of course,

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:07.140
very disappointing to see
the attack on scientists

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.560
and on science.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:09.730
And it's continued,

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:11.350
in fact, it's got stronger.

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:12.560
In this conversation,

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:14.510
you're going to hear about COVID,

00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:17.953
the Wuhan lab leak theory,
attacks on scientists

00:00:17.953 --> 00:00:19.973
and how we're gonna get out of this.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.903
Unimaginable loss, eye contact only,

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:41.083
longing for touch, push back.

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:45.283
The extraordinary becoming the ordinary.

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:48.930
COVID has changed everything

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:51.820
and we still know so little about it.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:53.720
Hello and welcome.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:54.740
My guest this week

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:57.500
is the World Health
Organization's chief scientist,

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:59.490
Dr. Soumya Swaminathan.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:01.190
Thank you for joining us.

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:03.860
Yes, thank you very much
for having me on your show.

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:05.340
The World Health Organization

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:09.743
was founded to guide global
public health policy in 1948.

00:01:09.743 --> 00:01:11.370
You are the chief scientist,

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:14.090
what a time to be the chief scientist.

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:17.621
I wanted to start by asking
you about the politicization

00:01:17.621 --> 00:01:19.980
of science and scientists.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.500
How have you found that?

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:24.370
Have you been surprised
by it during the pandemic?

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:25.203
In fact,

00:01:25.203 --> 00:01:27.440
that was one of the things
I was most surprised by.

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:30.910
It was completely
unexpected and of course,

00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:33.510
very disappointing to see the attack

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:35.840
on scientists and on science.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:37.030
And it's continued,

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:41.400
in fact, it's got stronger
over the course of the pandemic

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:44.300
and well, I think it has a potential

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:48.130
to do a lot of damage
and it's one of the areas

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:50.890
that I think we'll have to
think very seriously about,

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:53.810
going forward, not just
dealing with the pandemic,

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:58.520
but in general, when we are
trying to educate people

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:01.460
and for them to have more evidence

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:05.050
and data driven policies for countries.

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:09.490
I think that the element
of this kind of mistrust

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:14.100
and actual disinformation
will need to be addressed

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.000
and we need to work
with social scientists,

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:20.540
behavioral scientists and
as well as with communities

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:23.980
to really understand this whole phenomenon

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:25.510
and particularly young people,

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:27.220
I think we really need
to work with young people

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:31.050
to improve scientific
literacy, health literacy,

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.580
get them to think more rationally

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:35.250
to question information they see,

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:37.390
which just comes out the blue

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:39.440
and doesn't seem to be logical.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:41.760
So, the WHO has actually
launched a big program

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:45.500
of work in this area that we
call infodemic management.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:47.170
That's really looking
into the root causes,

00:02:47.170 --> 00:02:48.800
encouraging more research.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:51.630
It's a very multidisciplinary
area of work,

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:53.140
but certainly one of the challenges-

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:55.910
I was gonna say have you
personally faced attacks?

00:02:55.910 --> 00:03:00.492
I have and I've faced attacks
for just ordinary things,

00:03:00.492 --> 00:03:04.290
which I thought should
be non-controversial.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:06.040
So, making statements that are based

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:09.200
on the available evidence
and facts of that time

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.680
and of course we have to change

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.870
and evolve as data has been coming in.

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:14.790
And that's again I think
been one of the things

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:17.990
of the pandemic is that
we've had to change

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:20.620
and adapt our guidance as we go along.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:22.410
And perhaps that confuses people,

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:24.100
who don't understand how science works.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:28.230
And they may think that you were wrong

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:29.940
to say that a few months ago

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:31.850
or that you don't know
what you're talking about.

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:34.750
So, I think explaining
also the process of science

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:38.310
and that it's a continuous
learning, continuous evolution,

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:41.410
continuous questioning
and as more data comes in,

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:42.550
we must change our views.

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:45.104
Yes, I mean in terms of the attacks on you

00:03:45.104 --> 00:03:46.950
as information has changed,

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:47.870
how have they come to you?

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:49.560
Has it mainly been via social media?

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:51.470
Could you give me a flavor of that?

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:54.140
It's mainly been through social media

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:56.890
and I think, again this is
the first pandemic I think,

00:03:56.890 --> 00:03:58.850
in the social media age.

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:02.210
And so I've seen both the
positives and the negatives.

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:03.580
The positives of course have been

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:05.760
that you can get your messaging across,

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:09.395
that you get a lot of
information from the social media

00:04:09.395 --> 00:04:11.880
that you can be updated practically

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:14.220
in real time to what's
happening around the world.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:17.180
The downside is that you also get a lot

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:19.220
of false information out there.

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:22.100
And then you get these
communities of people

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:24.160
who organize themselves to attack.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:25.240
And that's what happened to me.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:28.740
I was attacked on social
media by a group of people,

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:31.480
for whatever their vested interest was.

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:32.770
I don't know what it is,

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:36.380
but they genuinely believed
that I was misinforming,

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:39.340
whereas I was communicating
the WHO guidance,

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:42.210
based on all of the data that we look at.

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:43.970
Do you get very frustrated by that?

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:46.600
You were one of the world's top scientists

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:48.260
and you're being accused of lying.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:51.750
I mean, when you go home
at night do you vent?

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:52.610
Do you get angry?

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:54.019
What's your reaction to that?

00:04:54.019 --> 00:04:56.700
It must be frustrating to say the least.

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:59.620
It is very frustrating and as I said,

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:02.530
I was extremely surprised
and very disappointed.

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:05.090
Yes, I mean of course and
that is the the wider focus,

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:06.970
you say of course it's
because of social media.

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:07.920
I think what you mean by that

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:10.290
is that's the way they
can get in touch with you,

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:13.010
of course as well as
reading other information,

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:16.090
but who do you blame
for the politicization

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:18.120
of scientists and science?

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:19.850
I think it's a combination of factors.

00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:22.010
I think it's the first time
that science has played out

00:05:22.010 --> 00:05:24.210
on the front pages of newspapers.

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:26.030
So in general, people are not used to,

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:28.900
I mean, when was the last
time that vaccine development,

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:30.993
was discussed by laypeople?

00:05:32.682 --> 00:05:34.420
There are hundreds of childhood vaccines

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:37.050
and other vaccines that have
been developed and used.

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:38.680
We've never gone step-by-step,

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:40.610
day-by-day into looking at these things.

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:43.700
So, I think one is the
understanding a process of science,

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:45.180
understanding about transmission.

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:48.480
All our understanding about
the virus has evolved.

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:51.280
And as that's evolved our
communication has changed,

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:52.380
our messaging has changed.

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:53.950
So, I think that's the first thing.

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:56.140
The second I think is the
issue that you brought up

00:05:56.140 --> 00:06:00.430
is about the environment of trust.

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:03.490
And you can see differences
between countries

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:05.160
in how much populations

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:08.540
and communities trust their
leaders and their governments

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:11.740
and how well governments have
communicated their messages,

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:13.120
how transparent they've been,

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:14.660
how they've explained to people.

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:16.000
Let's talk a bit more,

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:19.530
about the World Health
Organization then and trust levels.

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:21.180
A key question,

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:23.620
I bet you get asked this all the time.

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:25.560
How did COVID start?

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:28.170
What is your understanding
as the chief scientist

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:30.420
of the World Health Organization?

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:35.254
So, from historical experience

00:06:35.254 --> 00:06:37.862
we've seen that many

00:06:37.862 --> 00:06:39.930
or most viral infections

00:06:39.930 --> 00:06:42.500
that newly emerge have
been zoonotic infections.

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:46.130
So, they've come from an
animal host either directly

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:50.320
or through an intermediate
host to infect humans.

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:52.450
And starting from HIV,

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:56.503
from the Zika virus, from Ebola,

00:06:57.470 --> 00:07:00.140
from of course SARS and MERS,

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:04.600
the other two major coronaviruses
that have infected humans.

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:07.100
We've seen that they emerge from an animal

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:10.220
and then sometimes through
an intermediate host.

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:11.053
So, in this case,

00:07:11.053 --> 00:07:14.690
I think the genetic
sequences of this virus were,

00:07:14.690 --> 00:07:19.230
are still pointing towards
an origin, perhaps from bats.

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:23.040
That's the closest homology
that we found in sequence,

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:25.310
bats have a lot of coronaviruses.

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:28.820
And so, there's about 96, 97% similarity.

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:33.220
But I think what we haven't
got is the exact how,

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:38.160
when and where did that jump
happen from animals to humans?

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:39.630
And that's important to understand

00:07:39.630 --> 00:07:41.730
in order to prevent future pandemics.

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:44.220
Do you not think it's a bit
odd that we don't yet know?

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:46.590
It's not that odd
because even in the past,

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:48.930
it's taken many years
actually to understand

00:07:48.930 --> 00:07:51.820
the origin of viruses.

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:54.050
It takes several years to know

00:07:54.050 --> 00:07:55.840
that SARS came from civet cats

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:58.410
and MERS was spread from camels.

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:00.140
And similar early for HIV,

00:08:00.140 --> 00:08:02.003
it took a long time to understand

00:08:02.003 --> 00:08:05.710
that it came from chimpanzees in Africa

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:08.710
and the chimpanzee viruses then were able

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:10.070
to infect humans and changed.

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:11.605
If I may just intervene at that point,

00:08:11.605 --> 00:08:15.310
of course it's important
to bring up the idea,

00:08:15.310 --> 00:08:17.630
of the lab theory where
there's this concern

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:22.120
that it's been leaked from
a lab by accident or not

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:25.020
in China with scientists working in Wuhan.

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:27.680
Joe Biden has asked
United States Intelligence

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:28.513
to look into this.

00:08:28.513 --> 00:08:30.390
US Intelligence now
believe the virus escaping

00:08:30.390 --> 00:08:32.400
from a lab is at least credible.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:34.902
Have you ruled that out to the WHO?

00:08:34.902 --> 00:08:37.030
Nothing has been ruled out.

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:40.160
As you know we've had
this group of scientists,

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:43.090
an independent international
group of scientists

00:08:43.090 --> 00:08:44.450
that have been working on this,

00:08:44.450 --> 00:08:47.080
they've made two visits to China.

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:48.870
The last one was in February of last year,

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:51.350
there was a very detailed report

00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:54.140
that was presented with several options.

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:56.810
And clearly lab leaks can happen,

00:08:56.810 --> 00:08:58.060
have happened in the past.

00:08:58.060 --> 00:09:00.800
And one cannot rule it out.

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:01.890
So, one what one needs

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:04.360
is to look at the weight of the evidence

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:06.380
and the scientists who went to China

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:09.010
and worked with local Chinese researchers,

00:09:09.010 --> 00:09:13.970
felt that the most likely
scenario was the zoonotic,

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:15.290
the animal,

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:16.430
that it's come from an animal.

00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:17.810
Now, whether it's a wild animal,

00:09:17.810 --> 00:09:21.030
a domesticated wild animal
or a domestic animal,

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:22.940
but is it a bird or a bat?

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:23.870
That we still,

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:26.770
we don't know but the scientists,

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:29.090
the majority of them felt
that, that was the origin,

00:09:29.090 --> 00:09:30.330
but they didn't rule anything out.

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:33.867
They had it on the list
of hypotheses and said,

00:09:33.867 --> 00:09:35.847
"We need to examine all the data

00:09:35.847 --> 00:09:39.940
"and do more studies
in the field in China."

00:09:39.940 --> 00:09:41.520
You brought up the word trust

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:43.560
and World Health Organization,

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:46.500
last year in August the UK's
"Sunday Times Newspaper,"

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:48.040
published a damning investigation,

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:50.480
into what they call China's power grab

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:52.450
of the World Health Organization.

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:55.390
The key allegations amongst
that centered around the idea,

00:09:55.390 --> 00:09:58.090
having been embarrassed
by the SARS outbreak

00:09:58.090 --> 00:10:00.800
and the World Health Organization's
very public criticism

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:02.040
of China over that,

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:03.650
that officials from China,

00:10:03.650 --> 00:10:05.800
ever since have done as much as they can

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:08.127
to have as much control at the WHO.

00:10:08.970 --> 00:10:10.120
As the chief scientist of the WHO

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:12.860
what do you make of that allegation?

00:10:12.860 --> 00:10:13.693
I can tell you

00:10:13.693 --> 00:10:16.260
that there's no truth
behind those allegations.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:17.650
The World Health Organization,

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:20.240
first of all is made up
of its 194 member states.

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:21.073
And we are governed,

00:10:21.073 --> 00:10:24.370
in fact, we have now going
on in the building behind me,

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:25.890
the executive board,

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:28.210
where the of course the executive board,

00:10:28.210 --> 00:10:32.700
consists of 34 of the
member states that rotate.

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:34.780
They are the ones who make policy.

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:37.320
They determine the way that WHO works.

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:38.620
They set our priorities,

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:40.480
they agree on our funding.

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:45.160
And we then follow the program
of work that's set out.

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:47.400
We also, another thing that's
important to understand

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:50.920
is WHO works through global
networks of scientists.

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:53.770
And so we have thousands
and thousands of scientists

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:56.070
and researchers and doctors
from around the world

00:10:56.070 --> 00:10:58.020
who serve on our different committees.

00:10:58.020 --> 00:10:59.760
And they provide the recommendations

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:01.540
that go into our guidelines.

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:03.880
So, it's not just a
group of people in Geneva

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:06.700
who can be influenced by any country.

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:08.980
So, we try to be as open and transparent.

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:10.850
So, you feel satisfied

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:13.720
that there hasn't been any undue influence

00:11:13.720 --> 00:11:16.260
by the Chinese authorities over the WHO?

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:18.050
'Cause another reason I ask

00:11:18.050 --> 00:11:20.570
is you mentioned that fact
finding mission to China.

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:23.560
And I think this is very
important about trusting the WHO

00:11:23.560 --> 00:11:26.730
and continuing to have trust
in it as an institution.

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:27.780
Peter Ben Embarek,

00:11:27.780 --> 00:11:30.600
a Danish scientist who led
that fact finding mission

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:33.300
for the WHO into the
origins of COVID in China,

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:36.680
said the team was put under
pressure by Chinese scientists

00:11:36.680 --> 00:11:39.000
who made up half of
the investigating team.

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:41.840
He told journalists in August 2021,

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:43.990
that those Chinese scientists did not want

00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:47.140
the lab leak theory mentioned
at all in the report.

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:47.980
Now I must mention,

00:11:47.980 --> 00:11:49.510
he then retracted that statement,

00:11:49.510 --> 00:11:51.710
saying it had been mistranslated,

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:54.240
but he refused to comment further.

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:57.080
The issue is that doesn't
help with this perception

00:11:57.080 --> 00:11:58.970
that has built up with some

00:11:58.970 --> 00:12:02.800
that the WHO is too close to China

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:06.650
and hasn't been able to trust
what it's been told in China.

00:12:06.650 --> 00:12:08.640
So, we've said from the beginning

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:11.600
and this is why it's
important for countries now

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:14.910
that are going to negotiate
a pandemic treaty, right?

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:16.430
The special World Health Assembly

00:12:16.430 --> 00:12:18.600
that was held on the 1st of December,

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:20.970
came up with this report
called "The World Together"

00:12:20.970 --> 00:12:22.440
which is really looking at the future

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:24.270
and how do do we want it.

00:12:24.270 --> 00:12:26.920
I mean, things could
have gone much better.

00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:29.780
And what we need is for
countries to cooperate now.

00:12:29.780 --> 00:12:32.750
Tomorrow there may be a
new outbreak emergency

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.130
in some other country, right?

00:12:34.130 --> 00:12:35.200
We don't want the same thing

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:37.120
to be playing out over and over again.

00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:39.690
So, the world needs to come together.

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:44.230
The member states of the
WHO the 194 member states,

00:12:44.230 --> 00:12:47.340
need to come together to
agree on a set of rules.

00:12:47.340 --> 00:12:49.270
It's not WHO that can make the rules.

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:53.000
They need to make the
rules to give powers to WHO

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:54.540
to do the kind of investigations

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:56.270
that will benefit everyone.

00:12:56.270 --> 00:12:58.610
So, those are the kind of
discussions that will happen-

00:12:58.610 --> 00:12:59.880
That sounds, sorry if I may,

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:01.320
that sounds like you don't
think you've been able

00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:03.450
to do the investigations you can

00:13:03.450 --> 00:13:04.540
and a slightly different question

00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:06.240
is do you think China has been open enough

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:07.310
this time around with the WHO?

00:13:07.310 --> 00:13:09.570
It's about powers that WHO has.

00:13:09.570 --> 00:13:10.403
It's about the powers.

00:13:10.403 --> 00:13:14.190
So, we work with countries
in a collaborative manner.

00:13:14.190 --> 00:13:15.570
So, you need more power?

00:13:15.570 --> 00:13:17.310
Yes, I think more power,

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:20.040
especially to investigate outbreaks

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:22.800
that could lead to pandemics certainly.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:26.170
Do you think the WHO has been the leader

00:13:26.170 --> 00:13:27.590
it could have been at this time?

00:13:27.590 --> 00:13:29.170
There's also been some
criticism coming away

00:13:29.170 --> 00:13:30.387
from the China side

00:13:30.387 --> 00:13:32.570
for not declaring a
global health emergency,

00:13:32.570 --> 00:13:35.780
until the 31st of January,
I believe in 2020.

00:13:35.780 --> 00:13:37.790
Some people saying it's been too slow,

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:40.430
too cautious, not muscular enough.

00:13:40.430 --> 00:13:42.140
In fact, almost too collaborative

00:13:42.140 --> 00:13:44.820
to move to be a leader at this time.

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:47.020
Well, you can always,

00:13:47.020 --> 00:13:50.740
in retrospect I think that things,

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:51.860
could have been done differently

00:13:51.860 --> 00:13:53.530
or things could have been done better,

00:13:53.530 --> 00:13:56.920
but the fact is that when
a public health emergency

00:13:56.920 --> 00:13:59.080
of international concern was declared,

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:01.280
there were less than a hundred cases

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:05.170
of SARS-CoV-2 infection outside of China

00:14:05.170 --> 00:14:06.910
and no deaths had occurred.

00:14:06.910 --> 00:14:08.510
And again, I come back,

00:14:08.510 --> 00:14:09.720
it's the Emergency Committee

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:11.440
that advises the director general,

00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:13.600
whose recommendations the DG then follows.

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:16.140
So, when they first met
on the 23rd of January,

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:20.120
the majority felt that it was not time

00:14:20.120 --> 00:14:22.020
to declare a public health emergency

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:22.920
of international concern

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:25.790
and that the DG convened
them again a week later.

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:27.147
And that at that point they said,

00:14:27.147 --> 00:14:29.480
"Well, it looks like it is
spreading outside China."

00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:31.730
And they then made the recommendation.

00:14:31.730 --> 00:14:35.010
So, again it's a group of
scientists who looked at the data

00:14:35.010 --> 00:14:36.710
that was available at that time

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:38.730
and made the recommendation to the DG.

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:40.490
After that recommendation was made,

00:14:40.490 --> 00:14:42.420
the announcement on the 30th of January,

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:44.848
very few countries took it seriously.

00:14:44.848 --> 00:14:48.210
Most countries just went
about, you know, the normal,

00:14:48.210 --> 00:14:50.990
nobody was preparing
for what happened later,

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:54.240
a few weeks later in
Europe and then in the US,

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:56.470
because at that time, yes.

00:14:56.470 --> 00:14:59.450
So, valuable time was
lost between the time

00:14:59.450 --> 00:15:01.640
that the public health
emergency was declared

00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:05.620
and cases started climbing in
many of the Western countries.

00:15:05.620 --> 00:15:08.460
So, even though that was
a highest level of alert

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:10.350
that WHO can make.

00:15:10.350 --> 00:15:13.300
Just as I'm asking you about
the start of the pandemic

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:14.860
and the declaration of it.

00:15:14.860 --> 00:15:17.280
I think a lot of people wanna
hear about the end of it.

00:15:17.280 --> 00:15:21.300
They wanna know when
will we know it's over

00:15:21.300 --> 00:15:23.137
or certainly at a point where you can say,

00:15:23.137 --> 00:15:25.960
"We're not in a global pandemic."

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:27.740
What is that point?

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:29.760
So, I don't think anybody can predict

00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:32.362
when that point will come.

00:15:32.362 --> 00:15:35.070
We are looking at scenarios.

00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:37.470
And the scenario that
we hope will play out,

00:15:37.470 --> 00:15:39.490
will be that in 2022,

00:15:39.490 --> 00:15:42.500
we will have enough people
vaccinated around the world

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:45.080
to have that wall of immunity.

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:46.480
And we know now that the vaccines,

00:15:46.480 --> 00:15:47.880
we have currently are very good

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:50.300
at preventing severe disease and death.

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:52.880
And so if we can build that immunity,

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:54.940
which I have to remind everyone

00:15:54.940 --> 00:15:56.370
that 3 billion people around the world,

00:15:56.370 --> 00:15:58.250
still haven't had their
first dose of vaccine.

00:15:58.250 --> 00:15:59.540
I mean, that's shocking,

00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:00.400
even though we've had,

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:03.160
almost 10 billion doses
administered worldwide,

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:06.680
it could either circulate at
a low level, infect people,

00:16:06.680 --> 00:16:08.030
some people get ill,

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:10.280
but not a lot of people get severely ill.

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:14.350
It could also like influenza
have seasonal peaks

00:16:14.350 --> 00:16:17.760
in the future or there's
a bad scenario as well

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:21.700
that we might get another
variant after Omicron.

00:16:21.700 --> 00:16:24.970
That is not the mild variant,

00:16:24.970 --> 00:16:28.070
but we could get a variant
that's as transmissible

00:16:28.070 --> 00:16:29.310
or more than Omicron,

00:16:29.310 --> 00:16:31.730
but also is more virulent or more deadly.

00:16:31.730 --> 00:16:33.200
We can't rule that out.

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:35.070
And that's why we were saying,

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:37.870
let's not declare the pandemic over

00:16:37.870 --> 00:16:39.590
as some people are doing now.

00:16:39.590 --> 00:16:44.590
It would be foolish to
drop all our precautions

00:16:45.140 --> 00:16:46.650
that we've been taking all of this time.

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:48.050
We need to continue that.

00:16:48.050 --> 00:16:49.760
And hopefully by the end of 2022,

00:16:49.760 --> 00:16:51.070
we'll be in a much better position,

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:53.220
because let's remember this is a pandemic.

00:16:53.220 --> 00:16:55.720
So, one country cannot do something,

00:16:55.720 --> 00:16:59.020
without thinking that
they won't be affected

00:16:59.020 --> 00:17:01.540
by what goes on in
another part of the world.

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:04.220
A variant can arise anywhere and come back

00:17:04.220 --> 00:17:06.660
and you're back to square one.

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:09.810
So, I think it's good if the
whole world moves together,

00:17:09.810 --> 00:17:11.430
we still need to be cautious,

00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:14.260
but it's too early to
declare the pandemic over.

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:15.300
You just mentioned of course,

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:18.600
the billions of people who
don't even have a first dose

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:20.810
in their body of the vaccine.

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:22.160
What do you put that down to?

00:17:22.160 --> 00:17:24.080
Is it the situation with patents?

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:26.610
Is it the situation with countries,

00:17:26.610 --> 00:17:28.730
richer countries hogging vaccines?

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:30.410
What is the block there?

00:17:30.410 --> 00:17:32.700
Well, in one phrase if
you have to describe,

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:35.748
it's to vaccine inequity,
vaccine nationalism,

00:17:35.748 --> 00:17:38.100
it's a combination of the things you said.

00:17:38.100 --> 00:17:40.330
I think the beginning obviously vaccines

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:41.920
were in short supply.

00:17:41.920 --> 00:17:43.520
There were limited

00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:44.850
and it's incredible actually

00:17:44.850 --> 00:17:47.370
that vaccines even got developed in a year

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:49.750
and that we've had
billions of doses produced.

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:53.550
If those hundreds of millions
of doses we had in 2021,

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:56.020
had been distributed equitably,

00:17:56.020 --> 00:17:59.160
the way that the WHO had
laid out the framework,

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:00.970
let's protect all the vulnerable people,

00:18:00.970 --> 00:18:01.890
around the world first,

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:03.320
it doesn't matter where they live,

00:18:03.320 --> 00:18:04.820
so we can reduce deaths.

00:18:04.820 --> 00:18:07.500
And then we can start
vaccinating the other age groups,

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:10.920
coming down to adults and
adolescents and so on.

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:13.990
Then maybe we would not be
seeing new variants now.

00:18:13.990 --> 00:18:16.770
Maybe we would not be
still seeing 50,000 deaths

00:18:16.770 --> 00:18:18.460
a week today.

00:18:18.460 --> 00:18:20.110
Do you think the West,

00:18:20.110 --> 00:18:22.580
the richer countries hogging vaccines

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:24.350
has led to the variants?

00:18:24.350 --> 00:18:26.480
Yes, I think we can say that.

00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:30.290
85% of people in Africa
have not their first dose.

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:34.360
This is a recipe for letting
new variants develop,

00:18:34.360 --> 00:18:37.130
because a virus is transmitting unchecked.

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:38.880
And so I hope in 2022,

00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:42.000
that we can focus on bridging that gap.

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:43.630
Have you had COVID?

00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:44.463
Yes, I have.

00:18:44.463 --> 00:18:45.320
How was that?

00:18:45.320 --> 00:18:48.640
When was that in the pandemic
if you don't mind me asking?

00:18:48.640 --> 00:18:51.253
It was quite recent and it was,

00:18:52.300 --> 00:18:55.050
I was lucky that it was relatively mild

00:18:55.050 --> 00:18:58.250
and I could isolate at home
and self monitor myself

00:18:58.250 --> 00:19:00.340
and I felt better in about a week.

00:19:00.340 --> 00:19:01.500
Okay, because of course,

00:19:01.500 --> 00:19:04.060
so many more people now
have had the experience.

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:05.860
I just thought to ask you I suppose,

00:19:05.860 --> 00:19:09.930
how it was for you having
been working so hard on this.

00:19:09.930 --> 00:19:14.550
Yes, I must say that it was worrying,

00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:18.430
because I knows so much about
the paths that COVID can take,

00:19:18.430 --> 00:19:20.060
the complications that you can have

00:19:20.060 --> 00:19:23.260
and also the possibility of long COVID.

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:28.260
So, I think having been
vaccinated really did protect me.

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:30.250
Of course, I was taking
all the other precautions,

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:34.210
but still some times the
virus still gets to you

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:38.790
and I had, yes, mild, mild
symptoms I should say.

00:19:38.790 --> 00:19:41.240
And I kept working throughout actually,

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:42.520
even in isolation.

00:19:42.520 --> 00:19:43.530
I was able to do that.

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:45.010
Okay, well, I mean that's good to hear.

00:19:45.010 --> 00:19:46.280
We wouldn't wanna hear it any other way,

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:48.140
but I suppose it's just
when you work on something

00:19:48.140 --> 00:19:49.590
and then you experience it,

00:19:49.590 --> 00:19:52.970
it can change your view and
also your kind of understanding

00:19:52.970 --> 00:19:54.130
and your empathy levels with it.

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:57.740
And of course the reason this
has become so real to so many

00:19:57.740 --> 00:20:00.260
is because now more and more
people sadly know people

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:01.900
who've suffered very badly with it

00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:04.100
or sometimes in the worst
case lost loved ones.

00:20:04.100 --> 00:20:06.450
Has that happened in your life at all,

00:20:06.450 --> 00:20:07.900
have you lost anyone to COVID?

00:20:07.900 --> 00:20:08.733
Indeed.

00:20:08.733 --> 00:20:11.400
I mean, I think during the Delta wave

00:20:11.400 --> 00:20:15.146
that happened across the
world and in India last year,

00:20:15.146 --> 00:20:17.850
I lost many dear friends,

00:20:17.850 --> 00:20:22.570
classmates and family
members to COVID, yes.

00:20:22.570 --> 00:20:25.050
So, it did impact me also personally.

00:20:25.050 --> 00:20:26.529
I'm very sorry to hear that.

00:20:26.529 --> 00:20:27.410
Thank you.

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:28.920
It's just, I suppose the reality,

00:20:28.920 --> 00:20:30.410
we can talk all about the politics.

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:32.960
We can talk all about the
science, the lockdowns,

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:33.871
but at the end of the day,

00:20:33.871 --> 00:20:35.660
it's just for other people

00:20:35.660 --> 00:20:37.640
who I suppose haven't had
any exposure to the science,

00:20:37.640 --> 00:20:39.900
like you say we never used
to talk about epidemiology.

00:20:39.900 --> 00:20:41.980
We never used to talk about vaccines

00:20:41.980 --> 00:20:43.990
and then it just became so real.

00:20:43.990 --> 00:20:45.960
And how we get our heads around that,

00:20:45.960 --> 00:20:49.020
psychologically it's been very,
very difficult for people.

00:20:49.020 --> 00:20:51.040
And I imagine at the same
time as working on it,

00:20:51.040 --> 00:20:52.480
you've experienced that.

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:55.300
Exactly, I think so many of my colleagues,

00:20:55.300 --> 00:20:56.910
have been working around
the clock as well.

00:20:56.910 --> 00:20:58.247
We have to remember the
healthcare workers of course,

00:20:58.247 --> 00:21:00.330
who've have put themselves

00:21:00.330 --> 00:21:01.850
and that's why I said my classmates,

00:21:01.850 --> 00:21:06.850
doctors have died during
this pandemic, close friends.

00:21:06.950 --> 00:21:08.827
And of course people at WHO

00:21:08.827 --> 00:21:10.750
and all the other public health agencies

00:21:10.750 --> 00:21:11.750
and the ministries of health.

00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:13.810
So, it's had huge mental health impacts

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:15.530
on both on people who've been working

00:21:15.530 --> 00:21:18.150
and seeing a lot of
suffering on the front line.

00:21:18.150 --> 00:21:19.878
But of course also families,

00:21:19.878 --> 00:21:22.690
young people in particular.

00:21:22.690 --> 00:21:26.360
So, I think as we think about
coming out of this pandemic,

00:21:26.360 --> 00:21:29.920
we have to focus not just on
the health impacts of COVID

00:21:29.920 --> 00:21:32.240
and what we need to do to
build health system resilience,

00:21:32.240 --> 00:21:33.880
but on the broader economy,

00:21:33.880 --> 00:21:35.760
on inequalities in our society,

00:21:35.760 --> 00:21:37.250
which have really come to the fore.

00:21:37.250 --> 00:21:39.540
I mean, for me seeing some children

00:21:39.540 --> 00:21:40.600
that have been out of school

00:21:40.600 --> 00:21:42.803
for the last almost two years now,

00:21:43.760 --> 00:21:45.790
I really worry about their future,

00:21:45.790 --> 00:21:47.880
particularly poor children
who have not had access

00:21:47.880 --> 00:21:49.900
to online education

00:21:49.900 --> 00:21:52.180
and whether they'll be
into child trafficking

00:21:52.180 --> 00:21:54.780
or early marriages and so on.

00:21:54.780 --> 00:21:56.270
So, those are the kind of things I hope

00:21:56.270 --> 00:21:57.690
that countries will think about,

00:21:57.690 --> 00:21:59.790
thinking about the most vulnerable

00:21:59.790 --> 00:22:01.080
and how to protect them

00:22:01.080 --> 00:22:04.800
and how to build social
safety nets in the future.

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:06.640
Do you think we'll ever get over this?

00:22:06.640 --> 00:22:08.180
Of course we can get through it

00:22:08.180 --> 00:22:10.380
and hopefully get around it in some ways,

00:22:10.380 --> 00:22:12.340
but those ramifications,

00:22:12.340 --> 00:22:14.358
we're only just starting to think about,

00:22:14.358 --> 00:22:16.890
the social, educational,

00:22:16.890 --> 00:22:20.060
the impact on this
generation coming through.

00:22:20.060 --> 00:22:22.040
We will come through it,
we will get out of it.

00:22:22.040 --> 00:22:24.070
But I think it'll take longer than people,

00:22:24.070 --> 00:22:27.400
are currently planning.

00:22:27.400 --> 00:22:28.940
People think we'll be out of the pandemic

00:22:28.940 --> 00:22:29.840
by the end of the year.

00:22:29.840 --> 00:22:32.500
Yes, I mean the health
impacts of COVID hopefully,

00:22:32.500 --> 00:22:33.710
we will get over it.

00:22:33.710 --> 00:22:35.150
We're not going to get the virus.

00:22:35.150 --> 00:22:36.470
We will learn how to live with it,

00:22:36.470 --> 00:22:38.116
like with other respiratory viruses,

00:22:38.116 --> 00:22:41.620
but it's the other impacts
on the economy, on society

00:22:41.620 --> 00:22:42.960
and particularly on the vulnerable,

00:22:42.960 --> 00:22:45.090
this is the time to really start planning.

00:22:45.090 --> 00:22:46.270
And I particularly hope

00:22:46.270 --> 00:22:48.130
that we can keep children at the center

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:49.650
of this rebuilding.

00:22:49.650 --> 00:22:51.806
And the other thing is not
thinking about going back

00:22:51.806 --> 00:22:54.710
to how we lived in 2019,

00:22:54.710 --> 00:22:56.170
but to imagine a new future

00:22:56.170 --> 00:22:59.207
where we will continue to be very cautious

00:22:59.207 --> 00:23:04.050
and sort of looking at to see
whether there are new variants

00:23:04.050 --> 00:23:05.040
or viruses emerging.

00:23:05.040 --> 00:23:07.950
I think we have much better
surveillance systems globally

00:23:07.950 --> 00:23:09.570
as a result of this pandemic.

00:23:09.570 --> 00:23:11.180
And we can also put our masks on.

00:23:11.180 --> 00:23:12.013
We know that even

00:23:12.013 --> 00:23:14.680
if you've had an ordinary
respiratory infection or a flu,

00:23:14.680 --> 00:23:16.100
it's good to keep your mask on,

00:23:16.100 --> 00:23:18.000
because at least you're
not infecting your family

00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:18.833
and coworkers.

00:23:18.833 --> 00:23:20.280
So, I think we've learned a lot,

00:23:20.280 --> 00:23:22.020
we should take into the future.

00:23:22.020 --> 00:23:24.240
Thank you so much for talking to us.

00:23:24.240 --> 00:23:25.573
I think that's a very powerful point

00:23:25.573 --> 00:23:28.360
to bring our conversation to a close on

00:23:28.360 --> 00:23:30.770
with regards to how we might not go back,

00:23:30.770 --> 00:23:34.790
but there may be learnings
from this time to take forward

00:23:34.790 --> 00:23:37.140
and thank you for sharing the benefit

00:23:37.140 --> 00:23:39.270
of your research with us.

00:23:39.270 --> 00:23:40.320
Thank you.

00:23:40.320 --> 00:23:42.280
Thank you so much for being with us,

00:23:42.280 --> 00:23:43.340
until we meet again,

00:23:43.340 --> 00:23:45.133
stay safe and goodbye.

